{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03157",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 10.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second. What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.71,
      "end_seconds": 15.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "I've been coughing up large amounts of blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.04,
      "end_seconds": 19.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.61,
      "end_seconds": 33.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.04,
      "text": "It's a few times a day. Erm, I've also had a gurgling chest, since last night. I, I was feeling faint at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.35,
      "end_seconds": 39.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.16,
      "end_seconds": 45.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I haven't had fever, chest pain or weight loss, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.09,
      "end_seconds": 51.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Alright, anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.04,
      "end_seconds": 53.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.04,
      "end_seconds": 59.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "So, any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.62,
      "end_seconds": 63.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.67,
      "end_seconds": 80.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.64,
      "end_seconds": 84.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.38,
      "end_seconds": 88.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.19,
      "end_seconds": 94.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler. I take it once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.34,
      "end_seconds": 98.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.27,
      "end_seconds": 110.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "My partner and our baby. I hardly move around during the day. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.04,
      "end_seconds": 112.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.46,
      "end_seconds": 115.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 119.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.62,
      "end_seconds": 124.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "I've got COPD."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.08,
      "end_seconds": 131.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Yes, COPD is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.07,
      "end_seconds": 153.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.38,
      "end_seconds": 157.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.54,
      "end_seconds": 165.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.81,
      "end_seconds": 178.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.16,
      "end_seconds": 200.28,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 24, BP is 137 over 72. And pulse is 95 beats a minute, temperature is 36.9 degrees, oxygen saturation is 89 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.85,
      "end_seconds": 203.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.79,
      "end_seconds": 207.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Alright, don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.36,
      "end_seconds": 213.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.58,
      "end_seconds": 216.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.47,
      "end_seconds": 233.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "You are pale, breathing fast and bringing up fresh blood with every cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.85,
      "end_seconds": 236.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.16,
      "end_seconds": 253.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.2,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. From what you've told me and what I found, the most likely explanation is life-threatening haemoptysis. I can't rule out a pulmonary embolus yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.73,
      "end_seconds": 260.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.11,
      "end_seconds": 269.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like life-threatening haemoptysis, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.8,
      "end_seconds": 296.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "I'm going to order urgent blood tests, for bleeding. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 300.56,
      "end_seconds": 305.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "We have a slot Wednesday at 3:30 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.21,
      "end_seconds": 308.1,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.68,
      "end_seconds": 328.0,
      "duration_seconds": 18.32,
      "text": "Let's book an urgent CT scan to look into massive haemoptysis. I'll start you on tranexamic acid, 1 gram, now, single dose. That's for haemoptysis. Lie on the bleeding side and I am calling the emergency team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.51,
      "end_seconds": 333.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Sure. We'll catch up straight away. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.59,
      "end_seconds": 340.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}